course: dictionary
lesson: 3170
title: Empire: many lands, one ruler
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An empire is a large group of countries or lands that are all ruled by one ruler or one government. The ruler is often an emperor or an empress. «The empire was split into a western half ruled from Rome and an eastern half ruled from Constantinople.» Here one empire has two halves, and each half has its own ruling city.
explain: Empire can also mean a very large business, or a group of businesses, controlled by one person or company. «A toy empire» means a huge toy business that one person or company runs. Informally, an empire can be any area someone controls. «The kitchen is Dad's empire» is a joke: Dad is in charge of the kitchen.
explain: Context clues help you choose the right meaning. Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. In «The Ottoman sultan Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453, ending the Byzantine Empire», the Byzantine Empire must be a group of lands with one government, because that is what fits the sentence.
fact: Empire means a group of countries or lands ruled by one ruler or government.
fact: An emperor or an empress is often the ruler of an empire.
fact: «The Roman Empire» ruled the land where Jesus lived.
fact: Empires can rise and fall: they grow strong, and later they become weaker or break up.
fact: Italy became one state in 1861, and Germany in 1871, so many countries you know are younger than you think.
exercise: An empire is a group of countries or lands ruled by one ruler or government. What is an empire? | A small island with one school | *A group of countries or lands ruled by one government | A kind of bird with bright feathers
exercise: «The kitchen is Dad's empire.» In this sentence, what does empire mean? | *An area that someone controls | A very old church | A type of cake | A kingdom with a king in a castle
exercise: «A toy empire» is a very large business controlled by one person or company. Which meaning of empire is this? | A cold, wet day | A school for young children | A big country with an emperor | *A very large business
test: «The rise and fall of an empire» describes a time when an empire grows strong and then becomes weaker. What does rise and fall mean here? | Stays the same forever | Works hard on a building | Goes up a hill and down again | *Grows strong, then gets weaker
test: Why are the Ottoman, Aztec and Inca called empires? | Because they all built castles | Because they all had the same number of soldiers | Because they were all written about in the same book | *Because each ruled a large group of lands under one ruler or government
exam: Which sentence uses empire to mean a very large business? | The Roman Empire ruled the land where Jesus lived | Christianity spread across Europe | *Media empires are powerful companies that control many newspapers and television channels | Italy became one state in 1861
